      "chapterNumber": 2,
      "headline": "Aim High or Settle for Crumbs",
      "keyInsight": "Here is a strange quirk in how our minds work. If you enter a discussion hoping just to get by, your wish comes true. You get barely enough. There is a giant gap between a modest wish and a firm expectation. A wish is a vague daydream without roots. An expectation is a clear target backed by real conviction. When you set your target low, your brain stops looking for creative ways to build value. It locks onto the bare minimum and calls it a victory. But when you anchor your attention on a clear, ambitious goal, your brain hunts for solutions. The funny paradox is that high aimers do not just get better deals. They also walk away feeling energized rather than relieved to survive.",
      "content": "Imagine packing a backpack for a day of mountain hiking. If you pack only a single granola bar, you cannot climb past noon. Your stomach growls, your energy tanks, and you turn around early. Your initial preparation sets the outer limit for how far you can go. In negotiation, your target is that supply pack. Setting a low goal ensures you run out of fuel the moment the conversation gets tough.\n\nThink about asking for a home repair quote. A homeowner might think, \"I hope the contractor does not charge over five hundred dollars.\" That is purely defensive thinking. A prepared homeowner investigates material costs, checks standard labor rates, and sets an exact figure of four hundred. Now you are not merely reacting to someone else's opening number. You have built a solid dock where your boat can safely land.\n\nOptimistic targets work like magnets that pull your thinking upward. You cannot simply pull a wild fantasy out of thin air. Real targets must feel justified and honest in your own mind. When you truly believe your target makes sense, your posture straightens and your tone turns steady. Aiming high is not greedy. It is the simple engine that creates serious momentum.",
      "keyTakeaway": "Your clear expectations define the outer boundary of what you achieve.",
      "audioSnippetText": "Vague wishes leave you settling for whatever table scraps come your way. Specific targets give you the steady confidence to hold out for real value.",
